hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19213","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father who said: A man called Rabiah ibn Abbad from Banu al-Dil, and he was a Jahili, informed me, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Jahiliyyah in the market of Dhu al-Majaz, saying: O people, say there is no god but Allah and you will prosper, with people gathered around him, and behind him a fair-faced squint-eyed man with two braids saying: He is an apostate liar, following him wherever he goes. I asked about him, and they mentioned to me the lineage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said to me: This is his uncle Abu Lahab. Surayj narrated to us."
"19214","Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father from Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Duali, and he was a Jahili then embraced Islam, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. He said: I said: Who is this? He said: This is Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he is mentioning prophethood. I said: Who is this who belies him? They said: This is his uncle Abu Lahab. Abu al-Zinad said: I said to Rabiah ibn Abbad: You were then small. He said: No, by Allah, I was then discerning; I was carrying the waterskin, meaning bearing it."
